---
# `role-name` rejects a hyphen in a role directory name (`^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$`).
# Twelve roles here are hyphenated — claude-code, host-facts, agent-reach,
# multica-cli, oh-my-zsh, playwright-cli and the rest — and the names are load
# bearing: they match the upstream tool each role installs, they appear in
# main.yml, in every meta/main.yml `dependencies:`, throughout CLAUDE.md, and in
# the documented ad-hoc form `ansible localhost -m include_role -a name=host-facts`.
# Renaming twelve directories to satisfy a cosmetic rule would touch all of that
# for no functional gain, so the rule is skipped rather than obeyed. Every other
# rule stays on — the point is that `ansible-lint` exits 0 on a clean tree, so a
# NEW finding is visible instead of being lost among pre-existing ones.
skip_list:
  - role-name
